---
import { getEntries } from 'astro:content';
import { problemsInOrder } from '../../lib/content';
import { loadResearchLedger, ledgerEditionJsonHref } from '../../lib/research-ledger';
import { ledgerHref } from '../../lib/research-ledger-model.mjs';
import { pad,url } from '../../lib/site';
const ledger=await loadResearchLedger();
const problems=await problemsInOrder();
const rows=await Promise.all(problems.map(async p=>{
  const binding=ledger.input.manifest.currentSources.find((b:any)=>b.sourceKey===`problems/${p.id}`);
  const state=ledger.current.problemStates.find((s:any)=>s.recordId===binding?.recordId);
  if(!binding||!state)throw new Error(`Missing ledger problem state: ${p.id}`);
  return{p,binding,state,conds:p.data.conditions.length?await getEntries(p.data.conditions):[]};
}));
const counts=ledger.current.counters;
---
<section class="pr">
  <p>Current source capture: <time datetime={ledger.current.edition.capturedAt}>{ledger.current.edition.capturedAt}</time>. These are present states, not a completed annual result.</p>
  <div class="kpis">{[['Open',counts.open],['Partly answered',counts.partial],['Solved',counts.solved],['Under review',counts.underReview]].map(([label,count])=><div class="kpi"><div class="k-label">{label}</div><div class="k-value">{count}</div></div>)}</div>
  <p>No January baseline was recorded for the initial capture. Earlier states stay unknown. The ledger distinguishes dated editorial corrections, qualified research decisions, later support withdrawals and undated records.</p>
  <p><a href={url('/research-ledger/')}>Inspect the public research ledger</a> · <a href={url('/api/v1/research-progress.json')}>Exact progress JSON</a> · <a href={url(ledgerEditionJsonHref(ledger.current.edition.id))}>Complete pinned edition</a></p>
  <p>This capture records {counts.correctionArtifacts} editorial correction artifact affecting {counts.changedClaims} claims, {counts.qualifyingResearchResults} qualifying research results and {counts.peerReviewedManuscripts} manuscripts meeting the recorded peer-review gate. An editorial correction does not solve a research problem.</p>
  <div class="table-wrap"><table class="data"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Problem</th><th>Current state</th><th>Conditions</th><th>Source history</th></tr></thead><tbody>{rows.map(({p,binding,state,conds})=><tr><td class="num">{pad(p.data.number)}</td><td><a href={url(`/open-problems/${p.id}/`)}>{p.data.title}</a></td><td>{state.effectiveStatus}</td><td>{conds.map((c,i)=><>{i>0&&', '}<a href={url(`/diagnosis/${c.id}/`)}>{c.data.title}</a></>)}</td><td><a href={url(ledgerHref(binding.recordId))}>Exact record</a></td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
</section>
<style>.pr {margin-top:2rem;overflow-wrap:anywhere;}</style>
